From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:59:16 +0100
Subject: Remove Canada/East-Saskatchewan from the time zone abbreviations

timezonemap.h is from the bundled timezone database 2016.10 and still
lists Canada/East-Saskatchewan, which tzdata dropped in 2017c, so
timezone_abbreviations_list() returns a time zone that the system tzdata
does not have (ext/date/tests/bug51819.phpt). Upstream regenerated the
file in commit 8e3260376c6 ("Update timezonemap.h, which needs to match
the bundled TZ db", PHP 7.0.26); only the removal of this zone is taken.
---
 ext/date/lib/timezonemap.h | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/date/lib/timezonemap.h b/ext/date/lib/timezonemap.h
index 4147190..1683663 100644
--- a/ext/date/lib/timezonemap.h
+++ b/ext/date/lib/timezonemap.h
@@ -693,7 +693,6 @@
 	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "America/Thunder_Bay"           },
 	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "America/Winnipeg"              },
 	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "Canada/Central"                },
-	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "Canada/East-Saskatchewan"      },
 	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "Canada/Saskatchewan"           },
 	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "Mexico/BajaSur"                },
 	{ "cst",   0, -21600, "Mexico/General"                },
